{
  "result": "If I could only change one thing, I wouldn't pick something like ending a specific disease or solving climate change - as important as those are.\n\nI would give everyone the ability to truly *feel* what other people feel. Like, radical empathy.\n\nNot mind-reading, but deep understanding. To for a moment, really live inside someone else's experience - their fears, their hopes, their history, why they believe what they believe.\n\nI think so much of what breaks the world isn't that people are evil, it's that we just can't fully imagine each other. It's easy to hate, dismiss, hurt, or ignore someone when they feel abstract to you. It's almost impossible to do it when you viscerally understand their pain as if it were your own.\n\nIf everyone had that, I don't think war, cruelty, dehumanization, or even just everyday loneliness would survive for long. We'd still disagree - empathy doesn't mean we all agree - but we'd disagree like family instead of enemies. And from there, I think we'd actually *want* to solve hunger, poverty, and the climate crisis together, because we wouldn't be able to look away from each other anymore.\n\nThat's my one.\n\nWhat about you? What would you change?",
